  data:  # a201
    kind: work_item  # a201
    title: "python: a LAMBDA parameter escapes the LEGB shadow, so a lambda param shadowing a builtin could mint a fabricated builtin"  # a201
    status: todo_hard  # a201
    priority: 3  # a201
    parent:  # a201
    tags:  # a201
    - taint  # a201
    - python  # a201
    - analyzer  # a201
    isbefore: []  # a201
    duplicate_of: []  # a201
    not_duplicate_of: []  # a201
    pr_ref:  # a201
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-02 by reading INV-foluz's emitted rows back against source (PR #711).\n\nTHE FACT. py.py's bare-name emission arms refuse a callee bound anywhere in the\nLEGB chain, using the union of Scope.local_names over ScopeStack.frames. Scope's\nown docstring says \"One enclosing FUNCTION frame\", and the chain is built from\nast.FunctionDef nodes -- ast.Lambda is a different node type and contributes no\nframe. So a LAMBDA PARAMETER is invisible to the guard.\n\nTHE MEASURED SITE, and it is the only one. After the LEGB fix, hypergumbo-core's\n88,642 edges contain exactly ONE `external` bare-name row, and it is this shape:\n\n    packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_finalize.py:606\n    (lambda ctx, _o=orig, _n=name: (calls.append(_n), _o(ctx))[1])\n\n`_o` is a lambda parameter with a default; the call `_o(ctx)` emits\npython:external:0-0:_o:unresolved, asserting an external symbol for a value the\nlambda was handed. pretix's 102,927 edges contain zero instances.\n\nSEVERITY IS LOW BUT THE DIRECTION IS THE DANGEROUS ONE. Emitting a spurious\n`external` row is mild. The same hole in the BUILTINS arm is not: a lambda\nparameter shadowing a builtin --\n\n    sorted(xs, key=lambda x, len=my_len: len(x))\n\n-- would mint python:builtins:0-0:len, a FABRICATED BUILTIN, which is precisely\nthe StreamWriter defect the guard exists to prevent. Unmeasured whether that\nshape occurs in the corpus; it was not searched for.\n\nFIX SHAPE. Either give ast.Lambda a Scope frame in _pyscope (the honest fix, and\nit would also serve any other consumer of the LEGB chain), or union the lambda's\nown arg names at the call site. Prefer the first -- the second is a second home\nfor the same fact, which is the drift this file keeps rediscovering."  # a201
    fields: {}  # a201
- op: discuss  # 3696
  at: '2026-10-03T17:31:58Z'  # 3696
  by: agent  # 3696
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3696
  clock: 2  # 3696
  nonce: '3696'  # 3696
  message: "FIXED ON A LOCAL BRANCH, NOT MERGED (decontend run 10-03, together with INV-dulum-kakum-guhus-podas-mirup-lavut-jamob-kakif -- the same mistake): branch jgstern-agent/fix/dulum, commit 431c198905. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/dulum.md.\n\nFIX SHAPE TAKEN: the item's preferred one, in _pyscope, not a call-site union. ScopeStack.enter_subscope(names) returns a copy-on-write stack whose caller frame is extended with the lambda's (or comprehension's) names as locals and values; process_code_block passes it for the BODY only (defaults and a comprehension's first iterable stay in the enclosing scope). It is a frame EXTENSION, not a pushed frame, deliberately: a lambda contributes no Symbol, its calls are attributed to the enclosing caller, and frames[-1] is the caller's frame by contract (_caller_locals and the immediate lookups read it). Every LEGB-chain consumer -- the builtins arm, the external arm, the ORM-evaluating-builtin guard, lookup_enclosing, and now the import-map narrowing -- sees lambda parameters with no per-site code.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (live, analyze_python): sorted(xs, key=lambda x, len=my_len: len(x)) emitted python:builtins:0-0:len before, nothing after (sorted still emitted); (lambda c, _o=orig: _o(c))(ctx) -- the filed test_finalize.py shape -- emitted python:external:0-0:_o before, nothing after; lambda len: (lambda x: len(x)) (nested) refused; lambda len=len(xs): len still emits the REAL builtins len for the default (enclosing scope); lambda x: len(x) still emits builtins len (control). Tests: test_py_binding_scope_shadow.py::TestLambdaParametersShadow (RED 3 of 5 before the fix, the 2 controls green before and after); TestScopeStackEnterSubscope in test_pyscope.py.\n\nMEASURED: ast scan of 45,702 .py files: 0 lambdas call a parameter named like a builtin (the fabricated-builtin shape the title names); 51 lambdas call a non-builtin parameter (22 production) -- the python:external:0-0:<param> shape. django A/B: one such edge removed (tests/backends/base/test_base.py:168, a lambda's execute parameter)."  # 3696
