  clock: 4  # 8edc
  nonce: 8edc  # 8edc
  message: "Merged in PR #1438 (dev 81caa3999d). Integrated together: WI-kutal + WI-ratid (which restores the 2098 django edges kutal alone would have lost) + INV-dulum/WI-safit.\n\nFixed in PR #1438 (commit 431c198905), with INV-dulum (the same mistake). It takes the item's preferred shape, in _pyscope rather than a call-site union: ScopeStack.enter_subscope() extends a copy of the caller frame with a lambda's (and a comprehension's) names, for its BODY only. Every LEGB-chain consumer sees them. Behavioural evidence (analyze_python):\n- `sorted(xs, key=lambda x, len=my_len: len(x))` no longer emits python:builtins:0-0:len; sorted is still emitted.\n- The filed `(lambda c, _o=orig: _o(c))(ctx)` no longer emits python:external:0-0:_o.\n- A nested `lambda len: (lambda x: len(x))` is refused.\n- Controls hold: `lambda len=len(xs): len` still emits the real builtins len for the default, and `lambda x: len(x)` still emits it.\n\nCorpus scan: 0 lambdas in 45,702 files call a builtin-named parameter, and 51 call some other parameter. The shape the title fears is absent from this corpus; the external-placeholder shape is present."  # 8edc
